# MADAR ERP Engineering

- Preserve local-only data processing and configured `storage/` / backup roots. Never copy customer data, secrets, SQLite files, or backups into code bundles.
- Use the current SQLite drivers and conventions (`better-sqlite3` migrations/SQL and Sequelize integration). Migrations must be additive, transactional, versioned, registered in `schema_migrations`, and preserve existing IDs, relations, and history. Never recreate production schema or run destructive synchronization.
- Keep cash, inventory, invoice, payroll, and staff mutations transactionally consistent. Invoice creation is distinct from receipts/payments; main stock is whole units and reusable fractions belong to the secondary warehouse.
- Keep role checks and audit sensitive changes with actor, action, entity, before/after values, and timestamp. Deactivation must revoke login sessions and must not bypass outstanding tool-custody clearance.
- Keep archived originals byte-for-byte unchanged. Compress only derived image buffers; retain EXIF timestamp behavior and local file-root/symlink protections.
- Add focused tests using temporary SQLite databases and storage directories. Run relevant tests, `npm run check`, and `npm run build`; do not test against `system/data/madar.sqlite` or real `storage/`.
- Report implemented behavior separately from incomplete workflows, business-policy decisions, and unverified production readiness.
